Good Afternoon

Thank you for meeting with us on 16th October 2025 regarding Bridget Walker=
's invoices.

Please accept my apologies for the delay in replying.

Hopefully, you will have received a letter from the DWP regarding the highe=
r rate of Attendance Allowance.

I attach the original invoices that were issued prior to the Deferred Payme=
nt being set up and the credit note issued on 19th June 2023.

The 16th March 2023 Invoice had the 12-week disregard period from 27th Sept=
ember 2022 to 19th December 2022 the charges of =A34061.35 are correct. The=
 period 20th December 2022 to 5th March 2023 you were charged the =A3800.00=
 per week =A38,685.71 however, when the credit note was issued it reduced t=
his amount by =A3389.77 per week and the credit note for this period is =A3=
4231.19. Therefore the total amount due on this Invoice was =A38515.87.

The 14th April 2024 Invoice for a 4-week period 6th April 2023 to 2nd April=
 2023 the credit note reduced this period by =A31559.08, therefore =A31640.=
92 was due.

The 17th May 2023 for the period 3rd April 2023 to 30th April 2023 this ref=
lected the change in care homes and the uplift of charges at Westcliff Lodg=
e the credit note reduced the invoice by =A31408.85 to =A31659.37

The weekly amounts Deferred for each Care Home are as follows

Westcliff Lodge =A3389.77 when Care Home Cost was =A3800.00
Palmerston Care Home =A3386.30 when Care Home Cost =A3750.00
Palmerston Care Home =A3415.90 when Care Home Cost =A3800.03
Palmerston Care Home =A3449.27 when Care Home Cost =A3844.83

If you need any further information or would like to meet again to discuss =
this, please do not hesitate to contact me.

Kind regards,
Lynn Hyam -  Senior Finance Officer (Income)
